  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh Climate and Environment Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project description The project will support the scaling up of locally-led adaptation (LLA), nature-based solutions (NBS), and financing for adaptation. It will support activities of the GCA&#x2019;s Global Hub on LLA, focused on partnerships for scaling up proven LLA modules; knowledge sharing and acceleration focused on community needs; and capacity building for LLA. On NBS, the project will focus on a systemic approach for adaptation through three interconnected systems: resilient infrastructure networks; resilient cities; and resilient food systems. On climate finance, the focus will be on scaling up access to finance, including at the local level and in rural areas; promoting resilient financial ecosystems; and leveraging resilience of and resilience thorough SMEs in BangladeshThere is a possibility to enter multiple descriptions:- General description- Objectives- Target Groups-Others</narrative>
  </description>
